{
  "_about": [
    "How every route that takes a resource id is scoped to a tenant. One entry per",
    "'METHOD path' of tests/fixtures/rbac_route_permissions.json that has a path parameter;",
    "tests/test_tenancy_route_scoping.py fails when a route is missing here or listed twice.",
    "scope=workspace: the id names a resource owned by one workspace. The suite seeds one in",
    "  workspace A and calls the route as an administrator of workspace B: 404/403, nothing of",
    "  A's in the body, and A's resource unchanged.",
    "scope=platform: deployment-wide configuration or account administration. Called as the",
    "  same workspace-B administrator (not a platform administrator): 403/404, nothing changed.",
    "scope=exempt: the parameter is not a tenant-owned resource; 'reason' says why."
  ],
